{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1449398-momentum-in-aberrant","id":1449398,"title":"Momentum in Aberrant","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-05-23T17:22:55-07:00","id":1449398,"title":"Momentum in Aberrant","content":"I have just read through Aberrant and Trinity Core, considering running a campaign for my group. I have a question about Momentum as a mechanic in Aberrant, particularly hoping for feedback from folks who have played the game. <br /> <br /> How does the important of Momentum work in play in Aberrant, compared to the way it is written in Trinity Core? I am particularly thinking about the idea of Skill Tricks as the primary use for Momentum. Skill Tricks are obviously going to be a fairly big deal in a game where the players are largely talented humans; my question is whether that remains true in a game where players can toss tractor trailers and fly at supersonic speeds. Do Skill Tricks, and thus Momentum, matter as much? My worry is that it may feel a bit like an unnecessary appendage to the rules if the characters feel like it doesn't interact much with their powers.<br /> <br /> But I'm not sure whether this is an accurate read or not, so I'm curious what folks have found in actual play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2076-mrapophenia","name":"MrApophenia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-24T02:56:55-07:00","id":1449442,"title":"","content":"My experience running TC Aberrant is that momentum flows very well, more often helping rolls and not much with skill tricks, but they also have their moments.<br /> <br /> While in 1e, the rolls had huge numbers of dice and auto successes, in TC it is not true, and more often than you would believe you fail rolls (even with many enhancements attached to it, that you can\u2019t use if have no dice success), also many rolls are made of small pools, commonly Power + Quantum (if you are Q3 or less), and failing is even more common.<br /> <br /> Skill tricks are useful even for Novas, some cover details no power gives advantage or complement the powers.<br /> <br /> Finally, momentum is the main pay back aspect of Storypath. Conditions, even those of transformations grant momentum when get in the way of the characters, and so they compensate the group for the difficulties.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-24T06:25:37-07:00","id":1449451,"title":"","content":"I had somehow managed to entirely miss that you can just add Momentum directly to dice rolls - I had it in my head that all you used it for was Skill Tricks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2076-mrapophenia","name":"MrApophenia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-24T06:50:06-07:00","id":1449453,"title":"","content":"It's especially useful if you fail or botch a roll. You can add dice after the roll's results.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-25T03:56:56-07:00","id":1449527,"title":"","content":"Momentum is almost a necessity for a Q1 or 2 nova trying to max out, for that matter.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-30T05:56:34-07:00","id":1450306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aliasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1449398-momentum-in-aberrant?p=1449527#post1449527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Momentum is almost a necessity for a Q1 or 2 nova trying to max out, for that matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or reaching for more Flux.<br /> <br /> I have found that Momentum is less important to Aberrant. The players have more power and more options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10020,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10020-manifoldpersona","user":"Manifoldpersona","date":". 05-30-2021, 09:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10020-manifoldpersona","name":"Manifoldpersona","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T22:37:58-07:00","id":1450545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manifoldpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1449398-momentum-in-aberrant?p=1450306#post1450306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or reaching for more Flux.<br /> <br /> I have found that Momentum is less important to Aberrant. The players have more power and more options.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope.<br /> <br /> Flux gives you <i>enhancement</i>, not dice. Which means a Q1 nova still only has a 40% chance of maxing out successfully.<br /> <br /> Only Momentum will give you actual <i>dice</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-01T12:31:37-07:00","id":1450625,"title":"","content":"Honestly, using Momentum on a max out action is kind of a totally appropriate thing. &quot;Hey all so I plan on maxing out Quantum and want to use Momentum to add a dice to my Quantum 1 character.&quot; Not really something that I think should cause problem. <br /> <br /> Especially if you take Flux to give it an enhancement so that you can max out say both Quantum and a particular power or Mega-Attribute.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-01T12:45:13-07:00","id":1450629,"title":"","content":"The interesting thing about all the scale and enhancement Aberrants toss around is they don't always have large dice pools to back it up. It's pretty easy to roll 5 dice or less on an attack counting on the odds to give you one or two successes which then get a lot of enhancements added to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}